      "count": 1,
      "reason": "Consolidate the two existing origin/destination scan sites into the local driver pool fallback. Same origin-first and only-if-empty destination visits when the operation-local actor index is unavailable; the native indexed path reuses ordered candidates with live absence checks. No extra scan or repeated visit approved. Frozen 8980908 selector fixtures and native 150-day identity/pace proof renew the review."
    }
  ],
  "review20261010": "Growth scans are the unchanged original bodies split among housing/widen/vacancy/fabric. lvInputs gathers a complete current ordered building/street certificate; lvKernel traverses its copied streets only when that certificate changes. lvCold is the isolated original full algorithm for overridden helpers, not an extra native pass. Repeated certificates per standalone property query remain a measured optimization target; field-taking native aggregate helpers share one field without weakening freshness.",
  "review20261010Inspector": "Read-only detail cards: detailNaming makes one native-order settlement building pass on disposable copies, once per card, preserving sign uniqueness without changing world names. detailTollOwner reads existing world indexes; only a cold inspector without either index makes one folk pass into a local Map to resolve a payee without assigning ownership or warming the world. These are presentation-only scans, not new daily or transaction work; counts are limited to one site each.",
  "review20261011OpeningCapacity": "Direct-era opening only: initializeSimulation traverses the settlement entries once and each settlement's folk once to count actual household heads after native seeding. completeResidential sums initial physical housing capacity once, then increments it only for accepted native buildings. The optional missing-layout fallback counts surviving residential buildings once. No new daily or transaction traversal, per-candidate building-capacity recount or persistent population index. Native overlap and frontage checks remain authoritative.",
  "review20261011Institutions": {
    "source": "e3f6486 institution integration; reviewed introduced sites, not blanket approval of legacy transaction searches",
    "sharedOrderedIndexes": "craftIndex traverses native people/buildings once per revision/year/building-count change. Craft recruitment shares ordered trade candidates; grinding receipts are allocated once per market output and consumed by direct owner lookup. Scholar lodging and mint receipts reuse ordered room references, retaining live state, title and capacity checks. craftMintRoom has one native-order rebuilding fallback only after actual layout/compound/fabric invalidation or building-array change, never per ordinary receipt.",
    "dailyOrDatedWork": "technologyActors, learningRoster, tickLearning, tickAbbeys, churchPrepare/tickChurchBodies and freedomPrepare are native once-per-place actor/room boundaries. creditRefresh and creditAnnual retain dated native lender/obligation passes. Craft guild spending searches actual worthwhile repair work; research/benefit and available learning-room decisions inspect their current physical prerequisites. No new per-person transaction-wide grinding, mint or lodging scan is retained.",
    "vacancies": "governmentOfficer, mintOfficer, abbeyStaff, churchStaff, abbeyAppropriate, estateWorker, portHealthCandidate, technologyEquipmentTick, knightDubbing, tourneyProclaim, orderClergy, expeditionQuote, abbeyLaterLease and abbeyLeaseVacancies search actual native rosters only for an available paid office, staff vacancy, ceremony, voyage or lease, with actual funding/eligibility guards. Existing staff reuse direct identities and current contract checks.",
    "geometry": "Paid institution/castle/citadel/windmill/lock/courtyard/estate/abbey/new-town proposals and validation inspect actual current occupied geometry, native public access and entitled compensations. courtyardAccessValid uses the native spatial near-query with a cold-world building fallback. Castle surveys reuse pure polygons and operation-local work footprints; current native ordered certificates preserve exact terrain/title answers. Opening seedMarketStreet/laneSurvey/eduPlace and markSettlementBuilt remain physical opening or map-change work. millSluiceSlots is draw-only geometry.",
    "boundaryAndEvents": "Abbey capacity/buildings/crop/order findings/fabric, chivalric/military-order foundations and suppression, knight ceremonies and town rebuilding are conditional native physical/use/event passes. tickCourts searches heads only after actual owner/funds/site eligibility. Actual field/holder titles remain canonical; no anonymous purse or placeholder job is approved.",
    "inspectors": "learningSchoolsHTML, craftPlaceHTML, craftGuildsHTML and technologyEquipmentHTML operate on detached readonly inspector state, not daily authoritative decisions. They do not warm the worker world or throw simulation dice.",
